% ANEOS giant impact smoke test: differentiated Earth-mass body, forsterite
% mantle (68%) + iron core (32%), built with the Phase 17h HSE IC builder
% against the Stewart S19/S20 tables loaded through EOS_ANEOS.
%
% This default config has SELFGRAVITY_OFF and runs only a tiny fraction of a
% dynamical time. The companion Config_selfgrav.sh + aneos_giant_impact_selfgrav.params
% turns SELFGRAVITY on for the actual HSE validation gate.
%
%        HYDRO_MESHLESS_FINITE_MASS
%        SELFGRAVITY_OFF
%        EOS_ANEOS

InitCondFile                       aneos_giant_impact_ics
OutputDir                          output
TimeBegin                          0.0
TimeMax                            5.0
TimeBetSnapshot                    2.5
MaxSizeTimestep                    1.0
MinSizeTimestep                    1.0e-3
TimeBetStatistics                  1.0

BoxSize                            6.0e9
DesNumNgb                          32
MaxNumNgbDeviation                 0.1

CourantFac                         0.3
ErrTolIntAccuracy                  0.01
MaxRMSDisplacementFac              0.1

ErrTolTheta                        0.7
ErrTolForceAcc                     0.005

% CGS code units (matches Stewart .sesame tables).
UnitLength_in_cm                   1.0
UnitMass_in_g                      1.0
UnitVelocity_in_cm_per_s           1.0

SofteningGas                       1.0e7
SofteningHalo                      1.0e7
SofteningDisk                      1.0e7
SofteningBulge                     1.0e7
SofteningStars                     1.0e7
SofteningBndry                     1.0e7


ResubmitOn                         0
ResubmitCommand                    none

% ANEOS table parameters.
AneosNumMaterials                  2
AneosTable0                        forsterite.sesame
AneosTable1                        iron.sesame
